    {
      "id": "pt-condicional",
      "level": "B1",
      "title": "Condicional",
      "en": "Would and polite requests",
      "note": "The conditional adds -ia, -ias, -ia, -íamos, -íeis, -iam to the infinitive: falaria, comeríamos. Dizer, fazer and trazer use dir-, far- and trar-. It expresses a hypothetical result or future viewed from the past. In polite European Portuguese requests, queria and podia are also common: Queria um café, por favor.",
      "verbs": {
        "rows": [
