    {
      "id": "pt-conjuntivo",
      "level": "B1",
      "title": "Presente do conjuntivo",
      "en": "Wishes, doubt and necessity",
      "note": "The conjuntivo appears after many expressions of wishes, doubt and necessity: Quero que venhas; É importante que estudes. For regular -ar verbs use -e, -es, -e, -emos, -eis, -em; for -er and -ir use -a, -as, -a, -amos, -ais, -am. Common irregular forms include seja, esteja, tenha and vá. It is called subjuntivo in Brazilian Portuguese.",
